1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,971
In a study of ten popular crypto wallets, eight had no accessibility features.

2
00:00:05,921 --> 00:00:11,315
Blind users sent money to the wrong address, because nothing read it back.

3
00:00:11,566 --> 00:00:13,594
This is Readback.

4
00:00:13,544 --> 00:00:17,109
An accessibility-first way to use Solana.

5
00:00:17,109 --> 00:00:19,780
AI understands your request.

6
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:21,808
Code checks everything.

7
00:00:21,808 --> 00:00:23,426
You decide.

8
00:00:23,666 --> 00:00:26,050
There are no passwords.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,881
Your test wallet lives in your browser, or you can try a demo account with one click.

10
00:00:32,133 --> 00:00:36,043
I type: send zero point two SOL to Mum.

11
00:00:35,993 --> 00:00:39,783
Readback fills the form, but approves nothing.

12
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:46,111
The review reads back the contact, the full address, the fee, and the balance after.

13
00:00:46,111 --> 00:00:48,664
I confirm with a key press.

14
00:00:48,664 --> 00:00:53,177
This is the demo account, so nothing is sent to Solana.

15
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:56,317
It only pays saved contacts.

16
00:00:56,267 --> 00:01:00,188
It enforces a limit of half a SOL per payment.

17
00:01:00,188 --> 00:01:05,398
And when someone tries to talk it into sending everything, it refuses.

18
00:01:05,398 --> 00:01:07,423
AI can be fooled.

19
00:01:07,423 --> 00:01:09,780
It still can't move money.

20
00:01:10,033 --> 00:01:15,246
Lookalike addresses copy the first and last characters of one you trust.

21
00:01:15,196 --> 00:01:19,314
Readback flags them, and makes you confirm twice.

22
00:01:19,314 --> 00:01:24,788
It even spells addresses with letter case, because a screen reader won't.

23
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:28,759
Every screen works with a keyboard and a screen reader.

24
00:01:28,709 --> 00:01:31,498
Focus always lands where you are.

25
00:01:31,498 --> 00:01:34,327
Motion respects your settings.

26
00:01:34,327 --> 00:01:37,735
Text size and contrast are one switch away.

27
00:01:37,966 --> 00:01:40,033
AI understands.

28
00:01:39,983 --> 00:01:42,023
Code verifies.

29
00:01:42,023 --> 00:01:43,707
You approve.

30
00:01:43,707 --> 00:01:45,812
Solana settles.

31
00:01:45,812 --> 00:01:47,298
Readback.

32
00:01:47,298 --> 00:01:52,142
A Devnet prototype, built for the MLH Solana hackathon.